{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9b3cd9f3-3dc6-46f6-8f76-2626471ecde8","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Investigation Summary\n\n1. **Producer ([`catalog.build`](file:///workspace/catalog.py#L2-L3))**:\n   - Used [`canonical.key`](file:///workspace/canonical.py#L1-L2) to index entries.\n   - Originally did `value.strip().lower()`.\n2. **Consumer ([`query.get`](file:///workspace/query.py#L1-L3))**:\n   - Was doing direct lookup with `catalog.get(name.lower())`, bypassing [`canonical.key`](file:///workspace/canonical.py#L1-L2) and ignoring whitespace stripping.\n   - Also used standard ASCII `.lower()` rather than Unicode case-insensitive matching (`.casefold()`).\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- **[`canonical.py`](file:///workspace/canonical.py)**: Updated [`key`](file:///workspace/canonical.py#L1-L2) to use `value.strip().casefold()`, enabling full Unicode case-insensitive matching while stripping leading and trailing whitespace.\n- **[`query.py`](file:///workspace/query.py)**: Updated [`get`](file:///workspace/query.py#L2-L3) to use `key(name)` from [`canonical.py`](file:///workspace/canonical.py), making consumer lookup semantics fully consistent with producer catalog construction without modifying the stored catalog values.\n- **[`tests/test_query.py`](file:///workspace/tests/test_query.py)**: Added test cases covering whitespace trimming and Unicode casefold comparisons (e.g., German `ß`/`SS`, accented letters like `É`/`é`). All tests pass.\n","duration_seconds":50.637414838,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":180406,"output_tokens":1801,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":52517,"total_tokens":182207}}}
